        <definition>T Marmot::PhaseField::EnergyDegradationFunctions::quartic</definition>
        <argsstring>(const T pf)</argsstring>
        <name>quartic</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::PhaseField::EnergyDegradationFunctions::quartic</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const T</type>
          <declname>pf</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Quartic degradation function. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pf</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Phase field variable. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Numeric type (e.g., double, float). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Degradation function value.</para>
</simplesect>
This function is defined as <formula id="3">\[ g(\phi) = 4(1 - \phi)^3 - 3(1 - \phi)^4,\]</formula> where <formula id="1">$\phi$</formula> is the phase field variable. It represents a quartic degradation of the material stiffness as the phase field variable increases, providing an even smoother transition compared to the cubic function. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
